  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid Expansion Coffee Farm Mapping Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to rapidly expand the mapping of coffee farms in Vietnam to meet European Union Deforestation Regulation (EUDR) requirements. The EUDR is an EU law designed to prevent deforestation by ensuring that products sold in the EU, whether produced locally or internationally, are deforestation-free. This regulation requires Vietnam&apos;s coffee sector to adopt stricter sustainability and traceability practices, increasing costs for farmers while risking market access to the EU if compliance is not met.The project will contribute to the support for Vietnam to achieve a deforestation-free and transparent coffee sector in the long run and support ethnic minorities, the poor, and vulnerable groups, who make up 20% of the country&#x2019;s coffee farmers.It will deliver a comprehensive and actionable plan for scaling the coffee map (which shows all coffee plots and clearly distinguishes primary forest) and provide clear guidelines for expansion in the five Central Highland provinces. In addition, provincial and district level trainers will be trained in the necessary skills and knowledge to further train others, ensuring a multiplier effect in capacity building with the purpose of eventually completing the coffee map.</narrative>
  </description>
